nd have had at least one menstrual cycle.Does receiving government assistance disqualify me?No. A surrogate must demonstrate financial stability in order to qualify for the surrogacy program, however, receiving government assistance is not on its own a disqualifying factor.Ready to Begin Your Surrogacy Journey? You’ve learned what it means to be a surrogate—now it’s your turn to make a difference. When you partner with ConceiveAbilities, you’re supported, celebrated, and empowered from day one. Join the women who are helping build families and changing lives in the most meaningful way. Start Your ApplicationAdditional Resources Explore more topics and personal perspectives to support you wherever you are in your surrogacy journey. Surrogacy for Lactating MothersLearn how surrogates who choose to pump can provide continued care after delivery — and receive additional compensation for their time and effort.Surrogacy for Military WivesMilitary wives are uniquely positioned to be amazing surrogates. Discover how surrogacy can offer flexibility, purpose, and financial empowerment.Meet the Men Behind SurrogacySurrogacy isn’t just a women’s story — hear from the men who support, encourage, and stand proudly behind the journey.Lactation for New MothersUnderstand how lactation plays a role for intended mothers, and explore your options for feeding and bonding after surrogacy.Surrogacy in the Teaching CommunityMany teachers find surrogacy to be a natural extension of their nurturing spirit. Learn why educators make incredible surrogates.Surrogacy in the Nursing CommunityNurses bring compassion, expertise, and strength to surrogacy. See how their caregiving backgrounds make them ideal candidates for this life-changing journey.",
