    "content": "Title: Best Agency for Surrogacy in Washington State | Seattle, WA\n\nContent: Best Agency for Surrogacy in Washington State ConceiveAbilities is a leading surrogacy agency in Seattle, Washington, matching intended parents with surrogates throughout Washington and the Pacific Northwest. As one of the oldest surrogacy agencies in America, we’ve been at the forefront of a changing landscape alongside Seattle’s finest doctors and professionals. Our Seattle surrogacy agency has been providing third-party reproductive services to hopeful parents-to-be in Washington and around the world for twenty-four years and counting. For SurrogatesFor Surrogates Your Guide: Why Choose ConceiveAbilities? What Kind of Support and Compensation Will I Get with ConceiveAbilities? What Is the Process of Becoming a Surrogate in Washington? What Are Surrogacy Requirements in Washington? Frequently Asked Questions About Becoming a Surrogate in Washington State Related Blog Posts Why Choose ConceiveAbilities? As your local surrogate agency in Seattle, we are here to support every step of your surrogacy journey. From helping you do your research on the best Washington surrogacy agency to matching you with a family, ConceiveAbilities is honored to make your dream of being a surrogate come true. Seattle is home to some of the leading fertility clinics in Washington. As a tenured surrogacy agency in the Pacific Northwest, we have deep, long-standing relationships with the fertility clinics, doctors and surrogacy support staff throughout Seattle and across Washington state, making your journey as a surrogate in Washington one with great access to top-tier medical care and advanced fertility solutions. What Kind of Support and Compensation Will I Get with ConceiveAbilities? We offer a comprehensive All-In Surrogate Care and Compensation Program personalized for our Washington surrogates. We know timing, matching, and surrogate pay are priorities for you. That’s why we designed our program, which offers the best matches, highest pay, and most comprehensive support throughout your journey. About Our Care & Compensation ProgramWhat Is the Process of Becoming a Surrogate in Washington State? Becoming a surrogate mother in Seattle is a big commitment, but through our online application platform, we ensure your journey is safe and convenient, whether you live right in the greater Seattle area, Spokane, Tacoma, Vancouver, Bellevue, Kent, Kirkland, Everett, or another community in Washington. As a surrogate with ConceiveAbilities, below is a step-by-step look at our surrogate process: Apply to be a surrogate in Washington Find out if you qualify Match with intended parents Begin pregnancy Carry and deliver a baby Conclude your surrogacy journey Learn more about the surrogacy process here. What Are Surrogacy Requirements in Washington? Our surrogate requirements make sure your surrogacy journey is as healthy and successful as possible. Basic qualifications include: A long-term resident of the United States Between the ages of 21 and 43 at time of matching At least one healthy, uncomplicated full-term birth Frequently Asked Questions About Surrogacy in Washington State Is Surrogacy in Washington Legal?Yes. While Washington does not have a gestational surrogacy statute, gestational surrogacy is commonly completed in Washington. Courts have granted pre-birth orders for married couples, unmarried couples, and single individuals regardless of their sexual orientation. That said, it is important to note that the results can vary by county and specific documentation is required regarding the legal status of embryos. Working with ConceiveAbilities, you benefit from our long track record of success in Washington and can be confident about your surrogacy journey. Learn more about Washington Surrogacy Laws.How Do We Find Your Perfect Intended Parents in Washington?Our Matching Matters process sets us apart from other Seattle surrogacy agencies. We understand the significance of the right match, and we are proud of our Matching Matters process that focuses on the connection between a surrogate and the intended parent. Our experience has proven that matching does matter and our 97% initial acceptance rate proves it. The right match lays the foundation for the entire surrogacy process, resulting in a successful and rewarding experience. Often surrogates and intended parents, who start off as strangers to one another, become an extended part of one another’s families. For those who seek this depth of connection, and equally for those who don’t, ConceiveAbilities uses its Matching Matters to understand your goals and make matches that make sense.How Much Does Being A Surrogate Mother in Washington Pay?One of the most common questions we receive is, how much do surrogates get paid in Seattle? At ConceiveAbilities, our surrogate compensation package is one of the most generous, and well-planned, in the field. With ConceiveAbilities, we cover your needs upfront including location, insurance and incidentals. We also take into consideration your wage replenishment and qualifications that can increase your financial package. Take the first step to become a surrogate in Washington now!Who Can Become A Surrogate Mother in Seattle, Washington?Our surrogate requirements make sure your surrogacy journey is as healthy and successful as possible. Review these basic criteria to find out if you qualify as a surrogate candidate. Or, better yet, take our short personal assessment to see if you qualify to be a surrogate in Washington!Related Blog Posts Everything You Need To Know About SurrogacyNovember 3rd, 2021Surrogacy is rapidly growing as a way to grow families. In 2019, surrogates were part of 5.4% of all in vitro fertilization (IVF) procedures in 2019. Why? It is the most successful treatment for infertility, with a 75% success rate. That number can increase as high as 95% for a birth once the gestational carrier is pregnant. Read MoreConceiveAbilities Launches All-In Surrogate Care and Compensation Package!June 22nd, 2021Our surrogates tell you in their own words why they became a surrogate. And, if you have been thinking about becoming a surrogate, today may be the right time to begin your surrogacy journey. Post pandemic, intended parents, who have dreamt of building their family through surrogacy, are ready to take the next step. Now more than ever, surrogates are needed. If surrogacy is something that might fuel your purpose, we are here to help you learn about and answer that calling. Read MoreWashington State Legalizes Commercial SurrogacyMarch 16th, 2018Have you heard the fabulous news? Commercial Surrogacy is now legal in the state of Washington! We are very excited about this news and asked ConceiveAbilities' in-house Director of Legal Services & Client Advocacy, Meg Ledebuhr, to provide us with a little more clarity on this advancement. Read More",
    "source": "https://www.conceiveabilities.com/about/locations/surrogacy-seattle-wa/"
