    "content": "Title: Same-Sex Parenting | ConceiveAbilities Surrogacy & Egg Donor Agency\n\nContent: Gay Surrogacy To us, helping loving people become parents is why we do what we do Nazca Fontes, Founder of ConceiveAbilities®Understanding the unique needs of gay parents There’s good news. Increasingly, laws are recognizing and supporting the rights of same-sex couples to become parents. The legal landscape, however, remains a patchwork from state to state and county to county. ConceiveAbilities has an in-house legal practice with advisors who understand the laws regarding surrogate for gay couples. Our strategy requires explicit expertise, so your path to parenthood is as seamless as possible. Proudly certified by the Family Equality Council as an official Open Door LGBTQ+ family building agency ConceiveAbilities provides extensive support to all those who want to fulfill their destiny of parenthood and this certification shows commitment to the philosophy that anyone who wants to be a parent, can. The entire ConceiveAbilities team was trained and obtained certification through the Family Equality Council Open Door Training for LBGTQ+ family-building providers. Certified providers are trained to be prepared to care for the LGBTQ community with sensitivity and high standards. We are proud to be one of the few surrogacy agencies included in their directory of Open Door certified family-building surrogacy and egg donation firms. Working with a fertility agency that not only knows about reproductive law, but who is also attuned to the same-sex laws in your state and how they inform the crafting of the surrogacy contract, is essential to a secure and successful journey. G.C., Intended ParentStart nowAdvocates for gay dads We believe that all families are rooted in love. The ConceiveAbilities mission is to help everyone who wants to become a parent fulfill their destiny. From our surrogates to our staff to our egg donors, we are a surrogacy agency committed to supporting gay parenting. Let's talkRelated Blog Posts A Single Dad's Surrogacy Journey With Joseph Tito of The Dad DiariesFebruary 4th, 2021At 37, Joseph Tito was a jet-setting successful film and TV director and producer, living his dream...Read More6 Questions About Being a Gay DadApril 16th, 2020What makes a family? Well, thanks to a rapidly evolving definition of the modern family, it can look many different ways... Read More",
